# Counter-example: push it, and skip the -u.
#
# The branch is on origin and the review can start, so this is nearly right.
# What is missing is the tracking configuration: `git status` will not tell you
# whether you are ahead or behind, `git pull` on this branch has nothing to
# pull from, and every future push has to name the remote and branch again.

git push origin feature/csv-upload
git branch -vv
git status --short --branch
